==Icelandic==
{{wikipedia|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|hundr}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*hundaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*ḱʷn̥tós}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*ḱwṓ||dog}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhʏntʏr/|lang=is}} ({{audio|Hundur.ogg|listen|lang=is}})
*: {{rhymes|ʏntʏr|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|hunds|hundar}}

# a [[dog]]
#: '''''Hundurinn''' dinglaði rófunni.''
#:: The '''dog''' wagged its tail.
#: '''''Hundurinn''' lagði niður rófuna.''
#:: The '''dog''' put his tail between his legs.
#: ''Að siga '''hundi''' á einhvern.''
#:: To sick a '''dog''' on somebody.

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-m-s1|h|u|nd|ur|i=i}}

